clk: qcom: gcc-sm6375: let Venus switch the VCODEC0 GDSC to HW control

The vendor DT marks the VCODEC0 GDSC qcom,support-hw-trigger: the video
driver hands it to the hardware while the core runs. With HW_CTRL it is
in hardware mode from the start and dev_pm_genpd_set_hwmode() is not
supported, so Venus falls back to the WRAPPER_VCODEC0_MMCC_POWER_*
registers, which the AR50 Lite core does not have; on SM4375 (Xiaomi
Redmi Note 12 5G) the first encode session then hung the SoC. Use
HW_CTRL_TRIGGER as QCM2290 and SM6115 do for the same core.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6375.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6375.c
index f47dc2808..f4acd2044 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6375.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6375.c
@@ -3569,7 +3569,7 @@ static struct gdsc vcodec0_gdsc = {
 		.name = "vcodec0_gdsc",
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
-	.flags = HW_CTRL,
+	.flags = HW_CTRL_TRIGGER,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc hlos1_vote_mm_snoc_mmu_tbu_rt_gdsc = {
